10766: 31:0   Data
10767:                      RW   When the IOC_IACK_SC register is read, this field
10768: 
10769:                           contains an interrupt vector supplied by external logic
10770: 
10771:                           and is returned to the CPU. When the IOC_IACK_SC
10772: 
10773:                           register is written, this field contains the data for a PCI
10774: 
10775:                           special cycle.
10776: 
10777: 6.4.14 Initialization Requirements
10778: 
10779:             After the system power is turned on or after a reset condition (reset_in_l is
10780:             asserted), serial ROM (SROM) code must initialize the IOC registers.
10781: 
10782:             The SROM code does the following:
10783: 
10784:             1. Deasserts the rst_l signal by writing zero (0) to the IOC_SFT_RST register
10785:                   (Section 6.4.7).
10786: 
10787: 6-50 I/O Controller
10788:             2. Clears the ERR and LOST bits by writing ones (1's) to IOC_STAT0 register
10789:                   bits <5:4> (Section 6.4.3).
10790: 
10791:             3. Prevents the IOC from responding to itself by writing zero to the
10792:                   IOC_W_BASE1 and IOC_W_BASE0 registers (Section 6.4.9).
10793: 
10794:             4. Initializes the HAE<31:27> field in the IOC_HAE register (Section 6.4.1).
10795: 
10796:             This level of initialization is sufficient to allow CPU-initiated PCI transfers to
10797:             operate correctly. Boot code must do additional initialization to configure the
10798:             IOC such that it can respond to PCI-initiated transfers (DMA).

