10675: 6.4.12 Translation Buffer Tag Registers
10676: 
10677:             There is one translation buffer tag (IOC_TB_TAG) register for each TLB entry.
10678:             The IOC automatically updates these registers (IOC_TB_TAG7-0) when all of
10679:             the following conditions are met:
10680: 
10681:             � The TEN bit is set in the IOC_TB_ENA register (Section 6.4.6).
10682: 
10683:             � A PCI transaction hits in a PCI target window.
10684: 
10685:             � The WEN and SG bits are both set in the IOC_W_BASE register
10686:                   (Section 6.4.9) associated with the PCI target window.
10687: 
10688:             The IOC_TB_TAG registers can also be written directly for diagnostic purposes.
10689: 
10690:             See Section 6.3.3 for more information about the TLB.
10691: 
10692:             The IOC_TB_TAG registers can be accessed at the following addresses:
10693: 
10694: 6-48 I/O Controller
10695: Register              Address
10696: 
10697: IOC_TB_TAG0           188000000
10698: IOC_TB_TAG1           188000020
10699: IOC_TB_TAG2           188000040
10700: IOC_TB_TAG3           188000060
10701: IOC_TB_TAG4           188000080
10702: IOC_TB_TAG5           1880000A0
10703: IOC_TB_TAG6           1880000C0
10704: IOC_TB_TAG7           1880000E0
10705: 
10706: All bits of these registers are UNDEFINED after reset.
