10729: 6.4.13 Interrupt Vector and Special Cycle Register
10730: 
10731:             When the interrupt vector and special cycle (IOC_IACK_SC) register is read,
10732:             the IOC generates an interrupt acknowledge cycle on the PCI bus and returns
10733:             the vector data provided by external logic as the read data to the CPU.
10734: 
10735:             When the IOC_IACK_SC register is written, the IOC generates a PCI transfer
10736:             with a special cycle command code. The data written to the register is
10737:             transferred unmodified to the PCI bus and contains the special message data.
